#: ../../source/docs/common-servo.rst:5
#: 6c0e313ee28c480e9b7f576ae7da084d
msgid "Servo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo.rst:7
#: b869a229cc524411a915fbefc9df470e
msgid "Copter, Plane and Rover can control servos for any purpose, including: triggering a camera shutter, releasing a parachute or dropping a tennis ball.  These servo(s) can be controlled either directly by the pilot via a switch on the transmitter, through commands sent from the ground station or as part of a mission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo.rst:13
#: 3a189a79d26f4a2696ddf88e2b92565f
msgid "Either analog or digital servos may be used such as provided by ArduPilot partner `Hitec <https://hitecrcd.com/products/servos>`__ or other vendors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo.rst:16
#: 11e2f84e63d6452685e7f9cd800f7f3e
msgid "Connecting the servo to an AutoPilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo.rst:21
#: 292c0af2b4014a5fab5e87bfaca23e1e
msgid "If using Copter Connect the servo to AUX OUT 1, 2, 3 or 4.  MAIN OUT 1 ~ 8 should be avoided because these update at 400hz."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo.rst:23
#: 6bcc1e9e28ec40879c2e44ea9495b70d
msgid "If using Plane or Rover where all PWM outputs update at :ref:`SERVO_RATE<SERVO_RATE>`, which defaults to 50hz, any unused MAIN OUT or AUX OUT 1 ~ 4 may be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo.rst:25
#: 0528ea1517e6438f8813ea2c3a5e3085
msgid "AUX OUT 5 and 6 cannot be used by default because they are setup as :ref:`Relays <common-relay>`.  These pins can changed to Servo outputs by setting the ``BRD_PWM_COUNT`` parameter to 6 and setting :ref:`RELAY1_PIN<RELAY1_PIN>` and :ref:`RELAY2_PIN<RELAY2_PIN>` to -1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo.rst:29
#: 6b4fca3786f249138b2d3f2645231f9f
msgid "The Pixhawk autopilot cannot provide power to the servos so an external BEC or ESC that can provide 5V should be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo.rst:32
#: 8dc332f44d5c4a558baa8087f252b453
msgid "in firmware versions 4.2 and later, the method for setting a PWM/SERVO/MOTOR output to be a GPIO function is changed. Instead of ``BRD_PWM_COUNT`` being used, the individual ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` parameter is merely set to \"-1\". If set to \"0\", it remains a PWM output, unassigned to a function, and outputs that output's trim value when board safety is not active. If the servo function is being \"mirrored\" to a remote device, as in the case of a DroneCAN or KDECAN ESC, then in order to change the autopilot board's corresponding output pin to be a GPIO, but allow the ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` to still be assigned to the remote device, the :ref:`SERVO_GPIO_MASK<SERVO_GPIO_MASK>` parameter can be used to assign the board pin to be a GPIO without affecting the ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` assignment for the remote device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo.rst:34
#: 7e8c6e12e8ba4e40ab0580c18b6a03bf
msgid "when using digital servos they can provide faster and more precise control if a higher update rate for the PWM outputs is used by setting the :ref:`SERVO_RATE<SERVO_RATE>`  to a higher value such as 100Hz, 333Hz or even 400Hz, depending on the capabilities of the servos being used. This value affects **all** PWM outputs, other than motor control outputs, so only do this if all of the servos on the vehicle are digital servos that support this higher rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-servo.rst:37
#: fdeef95a58ab4300a53f31f00f14a486
msgid "Controlling the servo as a camera shutter"
